# Mandatory commit & push after agentic completion

This rule **overrides** any preference that says “only commit when asked.”

## Must commit + push
When an **agentic action completes** (implementation, fix, refactor, config, or any durable repo change), before ending the turn:

1. Check `git status`, `git diff`, recent `git log`
2. **If changes include `frontend/**` (or FE deploy/publish scripts):** run `cd frontend && npm ci && npm run build` first — **do not push** if the build fails (`specs/005-frontend-gha-dist/spec.md`)
3. Stage relevant files (never `.env` / secrets)
4. Commit with a concise why-focused message
5. `git push` to the tracked remote

Do this even if the user did not say “commit” or “push.”

## Must NOT commit/push
- **Plan-only turns**: Plan mode / Phase 1 / design checklist with **no** repo mutations
- **Explicit prompt opt-out** only: `no commit`, `don't commit`, `sin commit`, `no push`, `don't push`, `sin push`, `do not commit or push` (that turn only)

## Edges
- Clean tree → no empty commit; still verify status
- Hook failure → fix and new commit (no amend unless commit-safety rules allow)
- No force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested
- Never update git config
